we've been using the 2018 iPad pro since  it came out almost a year and a half ago  and one thing's for certain it's been  through a lot so let's examine the  history of this iPad pro and how our  personal thoughts on it have changed as  software has evolved and brought us into  2020 now we are expecting a new 20/20  iPad pro within the next couple of  months which we discussed in that video  which you can check out after this one  but I personally believe that the 2018  model is gonna sell like hotcakes even  after the 2020 model comes out let's  talk about why there are five main  features of this iPad pro that greatly  added to its success and they're also  the features that really matter for 2020  and beyond but before I get into these  features I want to quickly go through  how this iPad pro has evolved since  release in my very first review of the  2018 iPad pro less than two weeks after  release my thoughts were mostly negative  I mentioned that it was a mistake for  Apple to market the iPad pro as a  computer replacement when the software  was so limiting even though they added  the USB C port you couldn't connect a  flash drive or an external storage drive  file imports were limited to photos only  using an SD card adapter and it forced  you to use the Photos app to do it they  also added external display support but  it basically only mirrored your display  so you still have to touch your iPad to  control it because at that time there  was no Mouse support the 11 inch model  also had a brand new aspect ratio which  meant that most apps and games couldn't  use up the full display until they were  updated to specifically support the 2018  11 inch model and in terms of  performance even though the 2018 iPad  pro is much faster than the 2017 model  they both felt exactly the same because  they were barely any apps that could  utilize the 2018 models full power  so basically when this iPad pro was  released it honestly wasn't worth buying  and then came I pad OS which completely  changed the game for the iPad pro  external drives now work perfectly fine  allowing you to freely drag and drop  files to in from the iPad pro you can  even edit photos and videos  directly off of a drive without first  having to import it onto your iPads  local storage not only that but you can  now log on to a storage server  wirelessly using SMB we did this  ourselves and we were able to easily  access the files on our server apple  also updated split view so that you can  now open two instances of the same app  right next to each other making it a  whole lot more useful alongside that  they added new gestures for text  selection and undoing mistakes which  make it much easier to use Safari added  a new Downloads folder feature allowing  you to download PDFs and other files off  the internet and quickly use and edit  them Apple even added full keyboard  shortcut support so that using your iPad  smart keyboard actually felt like using  a MacBook a huge bonus for artists and  Apple pencil users was that the pencils  latency was reduced from 20 milliseconds  to only nine which made it feel even  more like a real pencil along with that  Apple finally added Mouse support now  while it's not perfect and it works  similarly to how touch controls work it  allows you to set your iPad aside when  using it with an external display these  new iPad OS features changed everything  about the iPad pro and has started to  make us question whether it could  actually replace a laptop so we compared  them to last year's base MacBook Air and  MacBook Pro our conclusion was that for  the first time ever the iPad pro  actually makes a lot of sense to buy  compared to a laptop it's got tons of  power and excellent display great  battery life great portability and it's  actually very functional with the new  iPad OS features giving you awesome  multitasking and file management  capabilities while also giving you  access to the massive database of iOS  apps and games and then came Mac OS  Catalina which allowed users to connect  their Mac to their iPad pro using the  new sidecar feature for things like art  and productivity so now here we are in  2020 and the great news is that since  the release of iPad OS the 2018 iPad pro  has continued to get better and better  now almost all apps that we've tried  support the  aspect ratio perfectly new apps like the  full desktop version a Photoshop are now  available and they do a great job of  supporting the iPad pro like for example  supporting the second-generation Apple  pencils new DoubleTap feature we've  noticed that more and more apps and  games are now utilizing more of the iPad  pros immense performance allowing users  to really feel the extra power not only  that but there are now more games that  support the iPad pros 120 Hertz display  like fortnight which recently added 120  FPS support to the 2018 iPad pro and let  me tell you it works incredibly well so  while it seemed ridiculous at launch  that Apple packed in so much power into  this iPad pro were actually extremely  glad that they did because it's still  very powerful even with the latest apps  and games that are being released today  and just recently Microsoft Outlook  finally added the long-awaited  side-by-side multitasking support so you  can now have two of the same Microsoft  app open side-by-side and if you look on  Amazon you'll see a bunch of USBC Docs  for the iPad pro really giving users  more freedom to connect whatever devices  they'd like to companies like Bridge are  now coming out with iPad pro keyboards  that feature track pads to make them  more and more like actual Mac books and  if Apple decides to add curser support  to a future iPad OS update these new  keyboards will be incredibly useful so  now that we know how drastically the  iPad pro has evolved since its release  let's get into the five main features  that I think really matter for 2020 and  beyond first off the main feature that  really sets the 2018 iPad pro apart is  the design the square edges in Slate  shape make it really unique compared to  any other iPad it's also the only iPad  to get rid of the home button and switch  to face ID giving us a display with even  bezels and rounded corners this makes  using this iPad pro a whole different  experience compared to using any other  iPad and that is what really matters  going into 2020 and if the rumors are  true about the 20/20 I phones coming  with a new square edge design the 2018  iPad pro is gonna feel perfectly at home  and not outdated at all the second main  feature that really matters is the  performance even though the new iPhone  11 Pro is using the latest Apple chip  it's actually still slower than the iPad  pro in both processor and graphics  performance it's actually so high that  even after a year and a half it can  easily chew through any app or game on  the App Store without any performance  issues so that gives us consumers a lot  of confidence going into 20/20 knowing  that we can truly rely on this iPad pro  the third main feature is the display  while most of the new higher-end ipads  come with the same retina quality  displays very low reflectivity an  excellent touch support the iPad pro  gets a major advantage and I'm not  talking about the brighter 600 nits  display compared to 500 on the others  but I'm talking about the fact that the  iPad pro gets the incredible once when  he hurts promotion technology this  basically means that the display can  dynamically adjust its own refresh rate  between 24 Hertz and 120 Hertz based on  the content you're viewing so if you're  watching a movie the display refreshes  at 24 Hertz which will save battery life  and if you're on the home screen or  playing a game with 120 FPS support  you're getting super fluid animations  that you just can't get on any other  iPad tablet or even macbook and seeing  as more apps and games are starting to  support 120 FPS this pro motion feature  is gonna get even better going into 2020  and beyond now the fourth feature is  actually the USB C port unlike any other  iPad the 2018 iPad pro is able to easily  connect to an external display using USB  C you can also buy a USB C dock and get  access to a bunch of ports that you  can't get on a regular iPad and what's  special about us PC is that it's able to  supply power to external flash drives  and storage drives allowing you to  easily transfer files which is much more  complicated on a lightning packin iPad  having this USB C port makes the 2018  iPad pro much more capable going into  2020 and it's gonna allow it to compete  with the upcoming iPad pro refresh much  easier than  it was still packing a lightning port  finally on to the fifth main feature  which admittedly isn't really a feature  but is still a really big deal and  that's the price we've seen this iPad  pro go as low as six hundred and  seventy-five dollars brand-new on Amazon  that's a whole 125 bucks off retail  price and in a couple of months when the  new model comes out there's a  possibility that it could drop even  lower maybe as low as six hundred to six  hundred and twenty-five dollars  brand-new and at that price you're  seriously getting so much bang for your  buck we're talking an iPad that's so  good that it competes with laptops so I  can imagine every 2018 iPad pro getting  snatched up off of Amazon as the new  2020 models come out because it's still  gonna be that good going into 2020 and  beyond so there you guys have it that's  our review of the 2018 iPad pro in 2020  if you enjoy this video go ahead and  check out that video right there of the  iPad pro playing fortnight at 120 frames  per second and if you're not already  subscribed click that circle above so  you don't miss out on our 20/20 iPad pro  coverage when it finally gets released  thank you guys for watching and we'll  see you in the next video  [Music]
 

